He's a player that's a little bit of small forward, a little bit of power forward, and

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:21.780
a lot of center.

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:26.180
The variety of things, let's look at the things that Brian Williams does to opposing teams.

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:29.920
We think his center is starting down low, but he will step out, set pick and roll.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:34.020
plays for the Chicago Bulls but eventually get himself back into the

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:38.760
paint area where we would expect a 6 foot 11 center to be able to finish off

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:43.200
plays in the paint close to the basket and Williams certainly is capable of

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:47.450
doing that. Then they will use him many times as a screener in the lane area to

00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:52.090
post up other people but after screening he finds the open pocket and turns into

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:56.230
that medium range jump shooter. What does that do to the opposing center? It

00:15:56.230 --> 00:15:58.190
It forces him to make a decision.

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:00.000
Do I lay back and protect the basket

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:03.660
or come out and defend that medium range jump shooter.

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:05.820
We then see Brian Williams with the ability

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:07.940
to step out away from the basket,

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:10.060
and after knocking out that jumper,

00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:13.600
